  "body": "## Summary\n- Stage a frozen noncanonical intake packet for The Crew: The Quest For Planet Nine.\n- Scope: physical Thames & Kosmos SKU 691868 base game and linked English manual.\n- Preserve official rules, independent reception, and three reduced source-linked visuals.\n\n## Evidence boundary\n- Official product page and manual are recorded as machine receipts.\n- Independent review evidence comes from Board Game Quest and The Family Gamers.\n- No BGG rating/weight is claimed; `game.weight` and `bgg_id` remain null.\n- Mission-by-mission and complete card-text denominators remain outside scope.\n\n## Verification\n- `validate-intake --run 2026-08-12-the-crew`: clean\n- prescribed Node intake/provenance suite: 47 total, 46 pass, 0 fail, 1 intentional skip\n- `validate-intake --base origin/main`: clean\n- visual suite: 5 pass, 0 fail\n- contact sheet inspected before delivery\n- `git diff --check`: clean\n- packet hash: `df702411e64c85618422e7ec87d6bb04c9ab203d10ad1021b784f74c52eb7661`\n\nThis is a Bathcat-authored pre-approval head. It remains OPEN + DRAFT + DO NOT MERGE. Mennonite must independently reopen every receipt and decide GO/HOLD/REVISE. Bathcat will not approve, promote, or merge.",
